       },
       "elements": []
      },
      {
       "id": "f694591",
       "elType": "widget",
       "widgetType": "text-editor",
       "settings": {
        "editor": "<p>Schnitz is an Australian fast-casual chain that does one thing really well: fresh, hand-crumbed schnitzels. The first store opened in Melbourne in 2002, and the brand has since grown to dozens of locations across Victoria, New South Wales, Queensland, South Australia and beyond.</p><p>Every schnitzel is crumbed in store and cooked to order. You can choose chicken, beef or a plant-based schnitzel, pick a crumb or a crumb-free flavour, and have it as a burger, a wrap, a salad or a plate with chips. That mix-and-match approach is why the menu can feel huge the first time you visit &#8211; and why a clear guide like this one is handy.</p><p>SchnitzMenu.com is an independent fan guide. We collect prices from public sources, store listings and delivery apps, mark every price as approximate, and refresh the data every month.</p>"
       },
       "elements": []
      },
